---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About PeptiBloom, the Scientific Library, its ownership and the principles that separate scientific evidence from commercial information."
>
  <section class="page-hero section">
    <div class="site-frame page-hero__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About PeptiBloom</p>
        <h1>A research-oriented ecosystem built around visible evidence and visible uncertainty.</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="page-hero__lead">
        PeptiBloom is being built as a scientific research library and research-oriented ecosystem. Scientific
        credibility, transparency and traceability take precedence over commercial persuasion.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--quiet" aria-labelledby="ownership-title">
    <div class="site-frame feature-layout">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Ownership</p>
        <h2 id="ownership-title">Ownership stays visible.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          The Scientific Library is a PeptiBloom initiative. Its relationship to PeptiBloom is shown clearly
          alongside the methods used to review and present scientific information.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="editorial-surface" aria-labelledby="promise-title">
        <p class="surface-kicker">Editorial reference</p>
        <h3 id="promise-title">Know what we know. Know what we don’t.</h3>
        <p>
          The library is designed to show not only conclusions, but also limitations, contradictions and open
          questions when they are part of the scientific picture.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="boundary-about-title">
    <div class="site-frame uncertainty-layout">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Clear boundaries</p>
        <h2 id="boundary-about-title">Science is not a disguised product page.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="uncertainty-pair">
        <article class="uncertainty-panel">
          <p class="surface-kicker">Scientific information</p>
          <h3>Evidence, limitations, sources and unanswered questions.</h3>
          <p>
            The public scientific experience is intended to help readers inspect the state of knowledge and the
            provenance behind it.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="uncertainty-panel uncertainty-panel--open">
          <p class="surface-kicker">Commercial information</p>
          <h3>Operational concepts remain a separate domain.</h3>
          <p>
            Products, SKUs, inventory, suppliers and batches do not become scientific evidence and are not
            connected to the library unless a future approved contract explicitly permits it.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft" aria-labelledby="current-scope-title">
    <div class="site-frame reading-column">
      <p class="eyebrow">Current scope</p>
      <h2 id="current-scope-title">Build the foundation before pretending the library is complete.</h2>
      <p>
        PeptiBloom’s first public foundation focuses on identity, methodology, transparency and the Scientific
        Library framework. Compound-level pages wait for an approved Evidence public contract and
        production-ready scientific content.
      </p>
      <div class="inline-links">
        <a class="editorial-link" href="/library/">Scientific Library <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="editorial-link" href="/methodology/">Methodology <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
